<sup><b>1</b></sup> Praise ye the LORD. Sing unto the LORD a new song, <i>and</i> his praise in the congregation of saints.<br />
<sup><b>2</b></sup> Let Israel rejoice in him that made him: let the children of Zion be joyful in their King.<br />
<sup><b>3</b></sup> Let them praise his name in the dance: let them sing praises unto him with the timbrel and harp.<br />
<sup><b>4</b></sup> For the LORD taketh pleasure in his people: he will beautify the meek with salvation.<br />
<sup><b>5</b></sup> Let the saints be joyful in glory: let them sing aloud upon their beds.<br />
<sup><b>6</b></sup> <i>Let</i> the high <i>praises</i> of God <i>be</i> in their mouth, and a twoedged sword in their hand;<br />
<sup><b>7</b></sup> To execute vengeance upon the heathen, <i>and</i> punishments upon the people;<br />
<sup><b>8</b></sup> To bind their kings with chains, and their nobles with fetters of iron;<br />
<sup><b>9</b></sup> To execute upon them the judgment written: this honour have all his saints. Praise ye the LORD. <br />
